// GENERATED by tools/embed-packages.mjs from hardware/ (do not edit here)
export const PKG_SOURCES = {"goal_pose_gui":{"README.md":"# goal_pose_gui\n\nA separate window, like `joint_state_publisher_gui`, for typing goal positions and orientations for any robot.\n\n| Robot | What the window sends |\n|---|---|\n| Arm with MoveIt | Tool pose (x, y, z, roll, pitch, yaw) or joint values to `move_group` (`/move_action`); a Cartesian (straight-line) path via `/compute_cartesian_path` and `/execute_trajectory` |\n| Arm without MoveIt | Joint values to `/<controller>/follow_joint_trajectory` (`-p use_moveit:=false -p controller:=arm_controller`) |\n| Mobile, legged, flying | Goal x, y (z), yaw to `/navigate_to_pose` (Nav2 or `pose_follower`); velocity sliders to `cmd_vel` |\n\n```bash\n# arm (MoveIt running)\nros2 run goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui --ros-args -p robot_type:=arm -p planning_group:=ur_manipulator -p end_effector_link:=tool0\n# mobile robot in Gazebo (DiffDrive system, plain Twist on /cmd_vel)\nros2 launch goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui.launch.py robot_type:=diff\n# mobile robot with Jazzy's diff_drive_controller (TwistStamped on its own topic)\nros2 launch goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui.launch.py robot_type:=diff stamped:=true cmd_vel:=/diff_drive_controller/cmd_vel\n```\n\nThe same goals from a terminal:\n\n```bash\nros2 action send_goal /navigate_to_pose nav2_msgs/action/NavigateToPose \\\n  \"{pose: {header: {frame_id: odom}, pose: {position: {x: 1.0, y: 0.5}, orientation: {z: 0.383, w: 0.924}}}}\" --feedback\nros2 topic pub --once /goal_pose geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped \\\n  \"{header: {frame_id: odom}, pose: {position: {x: 1.0, y: 0.5}, orientation: {w: 1.0}}}\"\n```\n\n`pose_follower` is a proportional controller with no map and no obstacle avoidance. Use Nav2 for real navigation.\nTests: `colcon test --packages-select goal_pose_gui && colcon test-result --verbose`.\n","config/pose_follower.yaml":"# pose_follower parameters (ros2 run goal_pose_gui pose_follower --ros-args --params-file ...)\npose_follower:\n  ros__parameters:\n    rate: 20.0            # control loop (Hz)\n    xy_tolerance: 0.05    # m: close enough to the goal position\n    yaw_tolerance: 0.05   # rad: close enough to the goal heading\n    k_linear: 0.8         # proportional gain, distance -> speed\n    k_angular: 2.0        # proportional gain, heading error -> turn rate\n    timeout: 120.0        # s: give up on a goal after this long\n    # max_linear and max_angular default from robot_type (diff 0.22 m/s, 1.5 rad/s: a TurtleBot3 Burger)\n","goal_pose_gui/__init__.py":"","goal_pose_gui/geometry.py":"\"\"\"Pure math used by the goal window and the pose follower (no ROS imports, so it is easy to test).\"\"\"\nimport math\n\n\ndef quaternion_from_rpy(roll, pitch, yaw):\n    \"\"\"Roll, pitch, yaw (rad, fixed axes X, Y, Z) -> quaternion (x, y, z, w), like tf_transformations.\"\"\"\n    cr, sr = math.cos(roll / 2), math.sin(roll / 2)\n    cp, sp = math.cos(pitch / 2), math.sin(pitch / 2)\n    cy, sy = math.cos(yaw / 2), math.sin(yaw / 2)\n    return (sr * cp * cy - cr * sp * sy,\n            cr * sp * cy + sr * cp * sy,\n            cr * cp * sy - sr * sp * cy,\n            cr * cp * cy + sr * sp * sy)\n\n\ndef rpy_from_quaternion(x, y, z, w):\n    \"\"\"Quaternion -> (roll, pitch, yaw) in rad.\"\"\"\n    roll = math.atan2(2 * (w * x + y * z), 1 - 2 * (x * x + y * y))\n    s = 2 * (w * y - z * x)\n    pitch = math.copysign(math.pi / 2, s) if abs(s) >= 1 else math.asin(s)\n    yaw = math.atan2(2 * (w * z + x * y), 1 - 2 * (y * y + z * z))\n    return roll, pitch, yaw\n\n\ndef wrap_angle(a):\n    \"\"\"Angle -> (-pi, pi].\"\"\"\n    return math.atan2(math.sin(a), math.cos(a))\n\n\ndef clamp(v, limit):\n    return max(-limit, min(limit, v))\n\n\nclass FollowerGains:\n    \"\"\"The pose follower's parameters (same names as config/pose_follower.yaml).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, max_linear=0.22, max_angular=1.5, xy_tolerance=0.05, yaw_tolerance=0.05,\n                 k_linear=0.8, k_angular=2.0, holonomic=False, fly=False, car=False, min_radius=0.6):\n        self.max_linear = max_linear\n        self.max_angular = max_angular\n        self.xy_tolerance = xy_tolerance\n        self.yaw_tolerance = yaw_tolerance\n        self.k_linear = k_linear\n        self.k_angular = k_angular\n        self.holonomic = holonomic\n        self.fly = fly\n        self.car = car                  # car-like (Ackermann): cannot turn on the spot\n        self.min_radius = min_radius    # m: the car's smallest turning radius\n\n\ndef follower_command(pose, goal, gains, aligning=False):\n    \"\"\"One step of the pose follower.\n\n    pose, goal: (x, y, z, yaw) in the same frame (odom).\n    Returns (vx, vy, vz, wz, aligning, done): a body-frame velocity, whether the robot is now only turning\n    to the goal yaw, and whether the goal is reached.\n    Differential robots turn towards the goal first, then drive while correcting the heading; holonomic robots\n    (mecanum, legged, flying) move straight to it and turn on the way. A car always rolls while it steers (forwards\n    or, for a goal behind it, backwards), its turn rate limited by its smallest turning radius; it reaches the goal\n    position, and the goal yaw is not enforced (a car cannot turn on the spot).\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y, z, yaw = pose\n    gx, gy, gz, gyaw = goal\n    dx, dy = gx - x, gy - y\n    dist = math.hypot(dx, dy)\n    dz = (gz - z) if gains.fly else 0.0\n    vx = vy = vz = wz = 0.0\n    if gains.car:\n        if dist > gains.xy_tolerance:\n            heading = wrap_angle(math.atan2(dy, dx) - yaw)\n            direction = -1.0 if abs(heading) > math.pi / 2 else 1.0\n            err = wrap_angle(heading + math.pi) if direction < 0 else heading\n            speed = max(0.3 * gains.max_linear, min(gains.max_linear, gains.k_linear * dist))\n            vx = direction * speed\n            wz = clamp(gains.k_angular * err, min(gains.max_angular, speed / gains.min_radius))\n        done = dist <= gains.xy_tolerance * 1.5\n        return (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, False, True) if done else (vx, 0.0, 0.0, wz, False, False)\n    if dist > gains.xy_tolerance and not aligning:\n        if gains.holonomic:\n            c, s = math.cos(-yaw), math.sin(-yaw)\n            bx, by = c * dx - s * dy, s * dx + c * dy\n            k = min(1.0, gains.k_linear * dist / gains.max_linear)\n            vx = bx / dist * gains.max_linear * k\n            vy = by / dist * gains.max_linear * k\n            wz = clamp(gains.k_angular * wrap_angle(gyaw - yaw), gains.max_angular)\n        else:\n            heading = wrap_angle(math.atan2(dy, dx) - yaw)\n            backwards = abs(heading) > 2.4 and dist < 0.4\n            err = wrap_angle(heading + math.pi) if backwards else heading\n            wz = clamp(gains.k_angular * err, gains.max_angular)\n            if abs(err) <= 0.5:\n                vx = clamp(gains.k_linear * dist, gains.max_linear) * math.cos(err) * (-1.0 if backwards else 1.0)\n    else:\n        aligning = True\n        eyaw = wrap_angle(gyaw - yaw)\n        if abs(eyaw) > gains.yaw_tolerance:\n            wz = clamp(gains.k_angular * eyaw, gains.max_angular)\n        if dist > gains.xy_tolerance * 3:\n            aligning = False\n    if gains.fly and abs(dz) > 0.03:\n        vz = clamp(gains.k_linear * dz, gains.max_linear)\n    done = (dist <= gains.xy_tolerance * 1.5 and abs(wrap_angle(gyaw - yaw)) <= gains.yaw_tolerance\n            and (not gains.fly or abs(dz) <= 0.04))\n    if done:\n        vx = vy = vz = wz = 0.0\n    return vx, vy, vz, wz, aligning, done\n","goal_pose_gui/gui.py":"\"\"\"goal_pose_gui: a window (like joint_state_publisher_gui) to type goals for any robot.\n\n  ros2 run goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui --ros-args -p robot_type:=arm -p planning_group:=ur_manipulator\n  ros2 run goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui --ros-args -p robot_type:=diff -p stamped:=true \\\\\n      -r cmd_vel:=/diff_drive_controller/cmd_vel\n\nrobot_type: arm | diff | ackermann | holonomic | legged | drone\n  arm     Pose tab: tool x, y, z (m) and roll, pitch, yaw (deg) in the planning frame -> MoveIt (/move_action,\n          or /compute_cartesian_path + /execute_trajectory for a straight line).\n          Joints tab: one slider per joint -> MoveIt joint goal, or (use_moveit:=false) straight to\n          /<controller>/follow_joint_trajectory.\n  others  Goal tab: x, y (z for drones), yaw in odom -> /navigate_to_pose (Nav2, or pose_follower from this package).\n          Velocity tab: sliders -> cmd_vel at 10 Hz (Twist, or TwistStamped with stamped:=true).\n\"\"\"\nimport math\nimport sys\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n\nimport rclpy\nfrom rclpy.action import ActionClient\nfrom rclpy.node import Node\nfrom rclpy.qos import DurabilityPolicy, QoSProfile\n\nfrom python_qt_binding.QtCore import Qt, QTimer\nfrom python_qt_binding.QtWidgets import (QApplication, QCheckBox, QComboBox, QDoubleSpinBox, QFormLayout,\n                                         QHBoxLayout, QLabel, QPushButton, QScrollArea, QSlider, QTabWidget,\n                                         QVBoxLayout, QWidget)\n\nfrom builtin_interfaces.msg import Duration as DurationMsg\nfrom control_msgs.action import FollowJointTrajectory\nfrom geometry_msgs.msg import Pose, PoseStamped, Twist, TwistStamped\nfrom moveit_msgs.action import ExecuteTrajectory, MoveGroup\nfrom moveit_msgs.msg import (BoundingVolume, Constraints, JointConstraint, MotionPlanRequest,\n                             OrientationConstraint, PositionConstraint)\nfrom moveit_msgs.srv import GetCartesianPath\nfrom nav2_msgs.action import NavigateToPose\nfrom sensor_msgs.msg import JointState\nfrom shape_msgs.msg import SolidPrimitive\nfrom std_msgs.msg import String\nfrom tf2_ros import Buffer, TransformListener\nfrom trajectory_msgs.msg import JointTrajectory, JointTrajectoryPoint\n\nfrom goal_pose_gui.geometry import quaternion_from_rpy, rpy_from_quaternion\n\nD2R = math.pi / 180.0\nSLIDER_STEPS = 1000\n\n\nclass GoalNode(Node):\n    \"\"\"All ROS communication of the window.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__('goal_pose_gui')\n        self.declare_parameter('robot_type', 'arm')\n        self.declare_parameter('planning_group', 'arm')\n        self.declare_parameter('planning_frame', '')          # '' = the root link of the URDF\n        self.declare_parameter('end_effector_link', '')      # '' = the last link of the group (from the SRDF)\n        self.declare_parameter('pipeline_id', 'ompl')\n        self.declare_parameter('planner_id', 'RRTConnectkConfigDefault')\n        self.declare_parameter('use_moveit', True)\n        self.declare_parameter('controller', 'arm_controller')\n        self.declare_parameter('stamped', False)\n        self.declare_parameter('frame_id', 'odom')\n        self.declare_parameter('max_linear', 0.5)\n        self.declare_parameter('max_angular', 1.5)\n        self.p = lambda n: self.get_parameter(n).value  # noqa: E731\n\n        latched = QoSProfile(depth=1, durability=DurabilityPolicy.TRANSIENT_LOCAL)\n        self.urdf_joints = []          # [(name, lower, upper, prismatic)]\n        self.root_link = 'base_link'\n        self.joint_positions = {}\n        self.create_subscription(String, 'robot_description', self._on_description, latched)\n        self.create_subscription(JointState, 'joint_states', self._on_joint_states, 10)\n        self.tf_buffer = Buffer()\n        self.tf_listener = TransformListener(self.tf_buffer, self)\n\n        self.move_group = ActionClient(self, MoveGroup, 'move_action')\n        self.execute_traj = ActionClient(self, ExecuteTrajectory, 'execute_trajectory')\n        self.cartesian = self.create_client(GetCartesianPath, 'compute_cartesian_path')\n        self.fjt = ActionClient(self, FollowJointTrajectory, f\"{self.p('controller')}/follow_joint_trajectory\")\n        self.nav = ActionClient(self, NavigateToPose, 'navigate_to_pose')\n        self.cmd_pub = self.create_publisher(TwistStamped if self.p('stamped') else Twist, 'cmd_vel', 10)\n        self.goal_pub = self.create_publisher(PoseStamped, 'goal_pose', 10)\n        self._goal_handle = None\n        self.status = lambda text: self.get_logger().info(text)   # replaced by the window\n\n    # ---------- robot model ----------\n    def _on_description(self, msg):\n        try:\n            root = ET.fromstring(msg.data)\n        except ET.ParseError as e:\n            self.get_logger().error(f'robot_description does not parse: {e}')\n            return\n        children = {j.find('child').get('link') for j in root.findall('joint')}\n        links = [link.get('name') for link in root.findall('link')]\n        roots = [name for name in links if name not in children]\n        self.root_link = roots[0] if roots else 'base_link'\n        joints = []\n        for j in root.findall('joint'):\n            kind = j.get('type')\n            if kind not in ('revolute', 'continuous', 'prismatic') or j.find('mimic') is not None:\n                continue\n            lim = j.find('limit')\n            lo, hi = (-math.pi, math.pi)\n            if kind != 'continuous' and lim is not None:\n                lo, hi = float(lim.get('lower', lo)), float(lim.get('upper', hi))\n            joints.append((j.get('name'), lo, hi, kind == 'prismatic'))\n        self.urdf_joints = joints\n\n    def _on_joint_states(self, msg):\n        for name, pos in zip(msg.name, msg.position):\n            self.joint_positions[name] = pos\n\n    def planning_frame(self):\n        return self.p('planning_frame') or self.root_link\n\n    def tool_pose(self, tip):\n        \"\"\"The tool's pose in the planning frame from TF, or None.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            t = self.tf_buffer.lookup_transform(self.planning_frame(), tip, rclpy.time.Time())\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - TF not there yet\n            return None\n        tr, q = t.transform.translation, t.transform.rotation\n        return (tr.x, tr.y, tr.z) + rpy_from_quaternion(q.x, q.y, q.z, q.w)\n\n    # ---------- arms: MoveIt ----------\n    def _request(self, vel, acc, time):\n        r = MotionPlanRequest()\n        r.group_name = self.p('planning_group')\n        r.pipeline_id = self.p('pipeline_id')\n        r.planner_id = self.p('planner_id')\n        r.num_planning_attempts = 1\n        r.allowed_planning_time = float(time)\n        r.max_velocity_scaling_factor = float(vel)\n        r.max_acceleration_scaling_factor = float(acc)\n        r.start_state.is_diff = True\n        r.workspace_parameters.header.frame_id = self.planning_frame()\n        for c, v in (('min_corner', -2.0), ('max_corner', 2.0)):\n            corner = getattr(r.workspace_parameters, c)\n            corner.x = corner.y = corner.z = v\n        return r\n\n    def plan_pose(self, xyz, rpy_deg, tip, execute, vel=0.5, acc=0.5, time=5.0, cartesian=False):\n        q = quaternion_from_rpy(*(a * D2R for a in rpy_deg))\n        pose = Pose()\n        pose.position.x, pose.position.y, pose.position.z = xyz\n        pose.orientation.x, pose.orientation.y, pose.orientation.z, pose.orientation.w = q\n        if cartesian:\n            return self._cartesian(pose, tip, execute, vel, acc)\n        frame = self.planning_frame()\n        pc = PositionConstraint()\n        pc.header.frame_id, pc.link_name, pc.weight = frame, tip, 1.0\n        sphere = SolidPrimitive(type=SolidPrimitive.SPHERE, dimensions=[0.001])\n        pc.constraint_region = BoundingVolume(primitives=[sphere], primitive_poses=[pose])\n        oc = OrientationConstraint()\n        oc.header.frame_id, oc.link_name, oc.weight = frame, tip, 1.0\n        oc.orientation = pose.orientation\n        oc.absolute_x_axis_tolerance = oc.absolute_y_axis_tolerance = oc.absolute_z_axis_tolerance = 0.01\n        req = self._request(vel, acc, time)\n        req.goal_constraints = [Constraints(position_constraints=[pc], orientation_constraints=[oc])]\n        self._send_move_group(req, execute)\n\n    def plan_joints(self, values, execute, vel=0.5, acc=0.5, time=5.0):\n        req = self._request(vel, acc, time)\n        req.goal_constraints = [Constraints(joint_constraints=[\n            JointConstraint(joint_name=n, position=float(v), tolerance_above=0.001, tolerance_below=0.001, weight=1.0)\n            for n, v in values.items()])]\n        self._send_move_group(req, execute)\n\n    def _send_move_group(self, req, execute):\n        if not self.move_group.wait_for_server(timeout_sec=1.0):\n            self.status('move_group is not running (/move_action). Start the MoveIt launch file first.')\n            return\n        goal = MoveGroup.Goal()\n        goal.request = req\n        goal.planning_options.plan_only = not execute\n        goal.planning_options.planning_scene_diff.is_diff = True\n        goal.planning_options.planning_scene_diff.robot_state.is_diff = True\n        self.status('Planning ...')\n        self.move_group.send_goal_async(goal).add_done_callback(self._on_move_group_accepted)\n\n    def _on_move_group_accepted(self, future):\n        handle = future.result()\n        if not handle.accepted:\n            self.status('move_group rejected the goal')\n            return\n        self._goal_handle = handle\n        handle.get_result_async().add_done_callback(self._on_move_group_result)\n\n    def _on_move_group_result(self, future):\n        res = future.result().result\n        code = res.error_code.val\n        self.status('SUCCESS' if code == 1 else f'MoveIt error code {code} (see the move_group terminal)')\n\n    def _cartesian(self, pose, tip, execute, vel, acc):\n        if not self.cartesian.wait_for_service(timeout_sec=1.0):\n            self.status('/compute_cartesian_path is not available (is move_group running?)')\n            return\n        req = GetCartesianPath.Request()\n        req.header.frame_id = self.planning_frame()\n        req.group_name, req.link_name = self.p('planning_group'), tip\n        req.start_state.is_diff = True\n        req.waypoints = [pose]\n        req.max_step = 0.01\n        req.avoid_collisions = True\n        for name, value in (('max_velocity_scaling_factor', vel), ('max_acceleration_scaling_factor', acc)):\n            if hasattr(req, name):        # added in later MoveIt 2 releases\n                setattr(req, name, float(value))\n\n        def done(future):\n            r = future.result()\n            self.status(f'Cartesian path: {r.fraction * 100:.0f} % of the way')\n            if execute and r.fraction > 0.99 and self.execute_traj.wait_for_server(timeout_sec=1.0):\n                goal = ExecuteTrajectory.Goal()\n                goal.trajectory = r.solution\n                self.execute_traj.send_goal_async(goal)\n        self.cartesian.call_async(req).add_done_callback(done)\n\n    def send_joint_trajectory(self, values, seconds):\n        if not self.fjt.wait_for_server(timeout_sec=1.0):\n            self.status(f\"No action server {self.p('controller')}/follow_joint_trajectory\")\n            return\n        goal = FollowJointTrajectory.Goal()\n        traj = JointTrajectory()\n        traj.joint_names = list(values.keys())\n        pt = JointTrajectoryPoint(positions=[float(v) for v in values.values()])\n        pt.time_from_start = DurationMsg(sec=int(seconds), nanosec=int((seconds % 1) * 1e9))\n        traj.points = [pt]\n        goal.trajectory = traj\n        self.fjt.send_goal_async(goal)\n        self.status(f\"Trajectory sent to {self.p('controller')}\")\n\n    def cancel(self):\n        if self._goal_handle is not None:\n            self._goal_handle.cancel_goal_async()\n            self._goal_handle = None\n            self.status('Goal canceled')\n\n    # ---------- bases ----------\n    def navigate(self, x, y, z, yaw_deg):\n        ps = PoseStamped()\n        ps.header.frame_id = self.p('frame_id')\n        ps.header.stamp = self.get_clock().now().to_msg()\n        ps.pose.position.x, ps.pose.position.y, ps.pose.position.z = float(x), float(y), float(z)\n        q = quaternion_from_rpy(0.0, 0.0, yaw_deg * D2R)\n        ps.pose.orientation.x, ps.pose.orientation.y, ps.pose.orientation.z, ps.pose.orientation.w = q\n        if not self.nav.wait_for_server(timeout_sec=1.0):\n            self.goal_pub.publish(ps)\n            self.status('No /navigate_to_pose server: published the goal on /goal_pose instead')\n            return\n        goal = NavigateToPose.Goal()\n        goal.pose = ps\n        self.status('Goal sent to /navigate_to_pose')\n        self.nav.send_goal_async(goal).add_done_callback(self._on_move_group_accepted_nav)\n\n    def _on_move_group_accepted_nav(self, future):\n        handle = future.result()\n        self._goal_handle = handle if handle.accepted else None\n        if not handle.accepted:\n            self.status('/navigate_to_pose rejected the goal')\n            return\n        handle.get_result_async().add_done_callback(lambda f: self.status(\n            'Goal reached' if f.result().status == 4 else f'Goal ended with status {f.result().status}'))\n\n    def publish_velocity(self, vx, vy, vz, wz):\n        t = Twist()\n        t.linear.x, t.linear.y, t.linear.z, t.angular.z = float(vx), float(vy), float(vz), float(wz)\n        if self.p('stamped'):\n            m = TwistStamped()\n            m.header.stamp = self.get_clock().now().to_msg()\n            m.header.frame_id = 'base_link'\n            m.twist = t\n            self.cmd_pub.publish(m)\n        else:\n            self.cmd_pub.publish(t)\n\n\ndef spin(label, lo, hi, step, decimals=3, value=0.0):\n    s = QDoubleSpinBox()\n    s.setRange(lo, hi)\n    s.setSingleStep(step)\n    s.setDecimals(decimals)\n    s.setValue(value)\n    s.setAccessibleName(label)\n    return s\n\n\nclass GoalWindow(QWidget):\n\n    def __init__(self, node):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.node = node\n        self.setWindowTitle('Goal Pose')\n        self.status = QLabel('')\n        self.status.setWordWrap(True)\n        node.status = self._status\n        layout = QVBoxLayout(self)\n        tabs = QTabWidget()\n        layout.addWidget(tabs)\n        layout.addWidget(self.status)\n        kind = node.p('robot_type')\n        if kind == 'arm':\n            tabs.addTab(self._pose_tab(), 'Pose')\n            tabs.addTab(self._joint_tab(), 'Joints')\n        else:\n            tabs.addTab(self._goal_tab(kind == 'drone'), 'Goal')\n            tabs.addTab(self._velocity_tab(kind in ('holonomic', 'legged', 'drone'), kind == 'drone'), 'Velocity')\n        self.resize(320, 480)\n\n    def _status(self, text):\n        self.status.setText(text)\n        self.node.get_logger().info(text)\n\n    # ----- arm: tool pose -----\n    def _pose_tab(self):\n        w = QWidget()\n        form = QFormLayout(w)\n        self.xyz = [spin(n, -5, 5, 0.01) for n in ('x', 'y', 'z')]\n        self.rpy = [spin(n, -180, 180, 5, 1) for n in ('roll', 'pitch', 'yaw')]\n        for n, s in zip(('x (m)', 'y (m)', 'z (m)'), self.xyz):\n            form.addRow(n, s)\n        for n, s in zip(('roll (deg)', 'pitch (deg)', 'yaw (deg)'), self.rpy):\n            form.addRow(n, s)\n        self.tip = QComboBox()\n        self.tip.setEditable(True)\n        self.tip.addItem(self.node.p('end_effector_link') or 'tool0')\n        form.addRow('Tool link', self.tip)\n        self.vel = spin('velocity scaling', 0.01, 1, 0.05, 2, 0.5)\n        self.acc = spin('acceleration scaling', 0.01, 1, 0.05, 2, 0.5)\n        form.addRow('Velocity scaling', self.vel)\n        form.addRow('Acceleration scaling', self.acc)\n        self.cart = QCheckBox('Cartesian path (straight line)')\n        form.addRow(self.cart)\n        row = QHBoxLayout()\n        for text, fn in (('Use current', self._use_current), ('Plan', lambda: self._plan(False)),\n                         ('Plan && Execute', lambda: self._plan(True)), ('Stop', self.node.cancel)):\n            b = QPushButton(text)\n            b.clicked.connect(fn)\n            row.addWidget(b)\n        form.addRow(row)\n        return w\n\n    def _use_current(self):\n        p = self.node.tool_pose(self.tip.currentText())\n        if p is None:\n            self._status(f'No TF from {self.node.planning_frame()} to {self.tip.currentText()} yet')\n            return\n        for s, v in zip(self.xyz, p[:3]):\n            s.setValue(v)\n        for s, v in zip(self.rpy, p[3:]):\n            s.setValue(v / D2R)\n\n    def _plan(self, execute):\n        self.node.plan_pose([s.value() for s in self.xyz], [s.value() for s in self.rpy], self.tip.currentText(),\n                            execute, self.vel.value(), self.acc.value(), cartesian=self.cart.isChecked())\n\n    # ----- arm: joints -----\n    def _joint_tab(self):\n        w = QWidget()\n        outer = QVBoxLayout(w)\n        self.joint_box = QVBoxLayout()\n        holder = QWidget()\n        holder.setLayout(self.joint_box)\n        area = QScrollArea()\n        area.setWidgetResizable(True)\n        area.setWidget(holder)\n        outer.addWidget(area)\n        self.joint_spins = {}\n        self.duration = spin('time', 0.5, 30, 0.5, 1, 3.0)\n        row = QHBoxLayout()\n        for text, fn in (('Load joints', self._load_joints), ('Use current', self._joints_current),\n                         ('Plan && Execute', self._send_joints)):\n            b = QPushButton(text)\n            b.clicked.connect(fn)\n            row.addWidget(b)\n        outer.addWidget(QLabel('Time (s), without MoveIt'))\n        outer.addWidget(self.duration)\n        outer.addLayout(row)\n        return w\n\n    def _load_joints(self):\n        while self.joint_box.count():\n            item = self.joint_box.takeAt(0)\n            if item.widget():\n                item.widget().deleteLater()\n        self.joint_spins = {}\n        for name, lo, hi, prismatic in self.node.urdf_joints:\n            s = spin(name, lo, hi, 0.005 if prismatic else 0.01)\n            s.setValue(self.node.joint_positions.get(name, 0.0))\n            slider = QSlider(Qt.Horizontal)\n            slider.setRange(0, SLIDER_STEPS)\n            span = (hi - lo) or 1.0\n            slider.setValue(int((s.value() - lo) / span * SLIDER_STEPS))\n            slider.valueChanged.connect(lambda v, s=s, lo=lo, span=span: s.setValue(lo + span * v / SLIDER_STEPS))\n            self.joint_box.addWidget(QLabel(f'{name} ({\"m\" if prismatic else \"rad\"})'))\n            self.joint_box.addWidget(s)\n            self.joint_box.addWidget(slider)\n            self.joint_spins[name] = s\n        if not self.joint_spins:\n            self._status('No /robot_description yet (is robot_state_publisher running?)')\n\n    def _joints_current(self):\n        for name, s in self.joint_spins.items():\n            s.setValue(self.node.joint_positions.get(name, s.value()))\n\n    def _send_joints(self):\n        values = {n: s.value() for n, s in self.joint_spins.items()}\n        if not values:\n            self._status('Press Load joints first')\n        elif self.node.p('use_moveit'):\n            self.node.plan_joints(values, True)\n        else:\n            self.node.send_joint_trajectory(values, self.duration.value())\n\n    # ----- bases -----\n    def _goal_tab(self, fly):\n        w = QWidget()\n        form = QFormLayout(w)\n        self.goal = {k: spin(k, -100, 100, 0.1) for k in ('x', 'y', 'z')}\n        self.goal_yaw = spin('yaw', -180, 180, 5, 1)\n        form.addRow('x (m)', self.goal['x'])\n        form.addRow('y (m)', self.goal['y'])\n        if fly:\n            self.goal['z'].setValue(1.0)\n            form.addRow('z (m)', self.goal['z'])\n        form.addRow('yaw (deg)', self.goal_yaw)\n        row = QHBoxLayout()\n        go = QPushButton('Go')\n        go.clicked.connect(lambda: self.node.navigate(self.goal['x'].value(), self.goal['y'].value(),\n                                                      self.goal['z'].value() if fly else 0.0, self.goal_yaw.value()))\n        cancel = QPushButton('Cancel goal')\n        cancel.clicked.connect(self.node.cancel)\n        row.addWidget(go)\n        row.addWidget(cancel)\n        form.addRow(row)\n        return w\n\n    def _velocity_tab(self, holonomic, fly):\n        w = QWidget()\n        form = QFormLayout(w)\n        self.vel_sliders = {}\n        lin, ang = self.node.p('max_linear'), self.node.p('max_angular')\n        axes = [('linear.x', 'vx', lin)]\n        axes += [('linear.y', 'vy', lin)] if holonomic else []\n        axes += [('linear.z', 'vz', lin)] if fly else []\n        axes += [('angular.z', 'wz', ang)]\n        for label, key, top in axes:\n            s = QSlider(Qt.Horizontal)\n            s.setRange(-100, 100)\n            s.setValue(0)\n            self.vel_sliders[key] = (s, top)\n            form.addRow(label, s)\n        self.publishing = QCheckBox('Publish at 10 Hz')\n        form.addRow(self.publishing)\n        stop = QPushButton('Stop (all zero)')\n        stop.clicked.connect(self._stop)\n        form.addRow(stop)\n        self.vel_timer = QTimer(self)\n        self.vel_timer.timeout.connect(self._publish_velocity)\n        self.vel_timer.start(100)\n        return w\n\n    def _value(self, key):\n        if key not in self.vel_sliders:\n            return 0.0\n        s, top = self.vel_sliders[key]\n        return s.value() / 100.0 * top\n\n    def _publish_velocity(self):\n        if self.publishing.isChecked():\n            self.node.publish_velocity(self._value('vx'), self._value('vy'), self._value('vz'), self._value('wz'))\n\n    def _stop(self):\n        for s, _ in self.vel_sliders.values():\n            s.setValue(0)\n        self.node.publish_velocity(0, 0, 0, 0)\n\n\ndef main(args=None):\n    rclpy.init(args=args)\n    node = GoalNode()\n    app = QApplication(sys.argv)\n    window = GoalWindow(node)\n    window.show()\n    timer = QTimer()\n    timer.timeout.connect(lambda: rclpy.spin_once(node, timeout_sec=0.0))\n    timer.start(20)\n    try:\n        code = app.exec_()\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        code = 0\n    node.destroy_node()\n    rclpy.try_shutdown()\n    sys.exit(code)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n","goal_pose_gui/pose_follower.py":"\"\"\"pose_follower: drives a mobile, legged or flying robot to a goal pose, without Nav2.\n\nSubscribes:  /goal_pose (geometry_msgs/PoseStamped)   -- e.g. RViz \"2D Goal Pose\", or the goal window\n             /odom      (nav_msgs/Odometry)           -- where the robot is\nAction:      /navigate_to_pose (nav2_msgs/action/NavigateToPose), the same interface as Nav2's bt_navigator\nPublishes:   cmd_vel (geometry_msgs/Twist, or TwistStamped with -p stamped:=true for Jazzy's diff_drive_controller)\n\nIt is a simple proportional controller: no map and no obstacle avoidance. Use Nav2 for that.\n\"\"\"\nimport math\nimport threading\n\nimport rclpy\nfrom rclpy.action import ActionServer, CancelResponse, GoalResponse\nfrom rclpy.callback_groups import ReentrantCallbackGroup\nfrom rclpy.executors import MultiThreadedExecutor\nfrom rclpy.node import Node\n\nfrom geometry_msgs.msg import PoseStamped, Twist, TwistStamped\nfrom nav_msgs.msg import Odometry\nfrom nav2_msgs.action import NavigateToPose\n\nfrom goal_pose_gui.geometry import FollowerGains, follower_command, rpy_from_quaternion\n\nROBOT_TYPES = {\n    'diff': dict(max_linear=0.22, max_angular=1.5, holonomic=False, fly=False),\n    'ackermann': dict(max_linear=0.6, max_angular=0.8, holonomic=False, fly=False, car=True),\n    'holonomic': dict(max_linear=0.4, max_angular=1.2, holonomic=True, fly=False),\n    'legged': dict(max_linear=0.5, max_angular=1.0, holonomic=True, fly=False),\n    'drone': dict(max_linear=0.5, max_angular=1.0, holonomic=True, fly=True),\n}\n\n\nclass PoseFollower(Node):\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__('pose_follower')\n        self.declare_parameter('robot_type', 'diff')          # diff, ackermann, holonomic, legged, drone\n        self.declare_parameter('stamped', False)              # publish TwistStamped (Jazzy diff_drive_controller)\n        self.declare_parameter('frame_id', 'base_link')       # header.frame_id of TwistStamped\n        self.declare_parameter('rate', 20.0)                  # control rate (Hz)\n        defaults = ROBOT_TYPES.get(self.get_parameter('robot_type').value, ROBOT_TYPES['diff'])\n        for name in ('max_linear', 'max_angular'):\n            self.declare_parameter(name, defaults[name])\n        self.declare_parameter('xy_tolerance', 0.05)\n        self.declare_parameter('yaw_tolerance', 0.05)\n        self.declare_parameter('k_linear', 0.8)\n        self.declare_parameter('k_angular', 2.0)\n        self.declare_parameter('min_radius', 0.6)             # m: smallest turning radius (robot_type ackermann)\n        self.declare_parameter('timeout', 120.0)              # s; a goal that takes longer is aborted\n\n        self._stamped = bool(self.get_parameter('stamped').value)\n        self._pub = self.create_publisher(TwistStamped if self._stamped else Twist, 'cmd_vel', 10)\n        self._group = ReentrantCallbackGroup()\n        self.create_subscription(Odometry, 'odom', self._on_odom, 10, callback_group=self._group)\n        self.create_subscription(PoseStamped, 'goal_pose', self._on_goal_pose, 10, callback_group=self._group)\n        self._server = ActionServer(self, NavigateToPose, 'navigate_to_pose', execute_callback=self._execute,\n                                    goal_callback=self._accept, cancel_callback=lambda _: CancelResponse.ACCEPT,\n                                    callback_group=self._group)\n        self._lock = threading.Lock()\n        self._pose = None           # (x, y, z, yaw) from /odom\n        self._topic_goal = None     # a goal from /goal_pose (no action client waiting)\n        self._aligning = False\n        self._active_handle = None\n        period = 1.0 / float(self.get_parameter('rate').value)\n        self._timer = self.create_timer(period, self._on_timer, callback_group=self._group)\n        self.get_logger().info(\n            f\"pose_follower ready ({self.get_parameter('robot_type').value}): /goal_pose and the \"\n            f\"/navigate_to_pose action -> cmd_vel ({'TwistStamped' if self._stamped else 'Twist'})\")\n\n    # ---------- inputs ----------\n    def _gains(self):\n        p = lambda n: self.get_parameter(n).value  # noqa: E731\n        kind = ROBOT_TYPES.get(p('robot_type'), ROBOT_TYPES['diff'])\n        return FollowerGains(p('max_linear'), p('max_angular'), p('xy_tolerance'), p('yaw_tolerance'),\n                             p('k_linear'), p('k_angular'), kind['holonomic'], kind['fly'],\n                             kind.get('car', False), p('min_radius'))\n\n    def _on_odom(self, msg):\n        q = msg.pose.pose.orientation\n        _, _, yaw = rpy_from_quaternion(q.x, q.y, q.z, q.w)\n        p = msg.pose.pose.position\n        with self._lock:\n            self._pose = (p.x, p.y, p.z, yaw)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _goal_tuple(pose_stamped):\n        q = pose_stamped.pose.orientation\n        _, _, yaw = rpy_from_quaternion(q.x, q.y, q.z, q.w)\n        p = pose_stamped.pose.position\n        return (p.x, p.y, p.z, yaw)\n\n    def _on_goal_pose(self, msg):\n        if msg.header.frame_id not in ('', 'odom'):\n            self.get_logger().warn(f\"Goal frame '{msg.header.frame_id}' is used as odom (no TF lookup here)\")\n        with self._lock:\n            self._topic_goal = self._goal_tuple(msg)\n            self._aligning = False\n        g = self._topic_goal\n        self.get_logger().info(f'New goal from /goal_pose: x={g[0]:.2f}, y={g[1]:.2f}, yaw={g[3]:.2f} rad')\n\n    def _accept(self, _goal_request):\n        if self._pose is None:\n            self.get_logger().warn('No /odom yet: goal rejected')\n            return GoalResponse.REJECT\n        return GoalResponse.ACCEPT\n\n    # ---------- control ----------\n    def _publish(self, vx, vy, vz, wz):\n        t = Twist()\n        t.linear.x, t.linear.y, t.linear.z, t.angular.z = float(vx), float(vy), float(vz), float(wz)\n        if self._stamped:\n            m = TwistStamped()\n            m.header.stamp = self.get_clock().now().to_msg()\n            m.header.frame_id = self.get_parameter('frame_id').value\n            m.twist = t\n            self._pub.publish(m)\n        else:\n            self._pub.publish(t)\n\n    def _on_timer(self):\n        # goals from /goal_pose are followed here; action goals run in _execute\n        with self._lock:\n            goal, pose = self._topic_goal, self._pose\n        if goal is None or pose is None or self._active_handle is not None:\n            return\n        vx, vy, vz, wz, self._aligning, done = follower_command(pose, goal, self._gains(), self._aligning)\n        self._publish(vx, vy, vz, wz)\n        if done:\n            with self._lock:\n                self._topic_goal = None\n            self.get_logger().info(f'Goal reached: x={pose[0]:.2f}, y={pose[1]:.2f}, yaw={pose[3]:.2f} rad')\n\n    def _execute(self, handle):\n        goal = self._goal_tuple(handle.request.pose)\n        self.get_logger().info(f'NavigateToPose goal: x={goal[0]:.2f}, y={goal[1]:.2f}, yaw={goal[3]:.2f} rad')\n        if self._active_handle is not None and self._active_handle.is_active:\n            self._active_handle.abort()\n        self._active_handle = handle\n        with self._lock:\n            self._topic_goal = None\n        aligning = False\n        start = self.get_clock().now()\n        rate = self.create_rate(float(self.get_parameter('rate').value))\n        feedback = NavigateToPose.Feedback()\n        result = NavigateToPose.Result()\n        try:\n            while rclpy.ok():\n                if handle.is_cancel_requested:\n                    self._publish(0, 0, 0, 0)\n                    handle.canceled()\n                    return result\n                if not handle.is_active:          # replaced by a newer goal\n                    return result\n                with self._lock:\n                    pose = self._pose\n                vx, vy, vz, wz, aligning, done = follower_command(pose, goal, self._gains(), aligning)\n                self._publish(vx, vy, vz, wz)\n                elapsed = (self.get_clock().now() - start).nanoseconds * 1e-9\n                feedback.current_pose.header.frame_id = 'odom'\n                feedback.current_pose.pose.position.x, feedback.current_pose.pose.position.y = pose[0], pose[1]\n                feedback.distance_remaining = float(math.hypot(goal[0] - pose[0], goal[1] - pose[1]))\n                feedback.navigation_time.sec = int(elapsed)\n                handle.publish_feedback(feedback)\n                if done:\n                    handle.succeed()\n                    self.get_logger().info('Goal reached')\n                    return result\n                if elapsed > float(self.get_parameter('timeout').value):\n                    self._publish(0, 0, 0, 0)\n                    result.error_code = 9  # NavigateToPose has only NONE=0 in Jazzy; a non-zero code marks a failure\n                    result.error_msg = 'timeout'\n                    handle.abort()\n                    return result\n                rate.sleep()\n        finally:\n            if self._active_handle is handle:\n                self._active_handle = None\n        return result\n\n\ndef main(args=None):\n    rclpy.init(args=args)\n    node = PoseFollower()\n    executor = MultiThreadedExecutor(num_threads=3)\n    executor.add_node(node)\n    try:\n        executor.spin()\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        pass\n    finally:\n        node._publish(0, 0, 0, 0)\n        node.destroy_node()\n        rclpy.try_shutdown()\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n","launch/goal_pose_gui.launch.py":"\"\"\"The goal window, plus the pose follower for robots that move around (no Nav2 needed).\n\n  ros2 launch goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui.launch.py robot_type:=arm planning_group:=ur_manipulator\n  ros2 launch goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui.launch.py robot_type:=diff\n  ros2 launch goal_pose_gui goal_pose_gui.launch.py robot_type:=diff stamped:=true cmd_vel:=/diff_drive_controller/cmd_vel\n\"\"\"\nimport os\n\nfrom ament_index_python.packages import get_package_share_directory\nfrom launch import LaunchDescription\nfrom launch.actions import DeclareLaunchArgument\nfrom launch.conditions import UnlessCondition\nfrom launch.substitutions import LaunchConfiguration, PythonExpression\nfrom launch_ros.actions import Node\nfrom launch_ros.parameter_descriptions import ParameterValue\n\n\ndef generate_launch_description():\n    robot_type = LaunchConfiguration('robot_type')\n    stamped = ParameterValue(LaunchConfiguration('stamped'), value_type=bool)\n    sim_time = ParameterValue(LaunchConfiguration('use_sim_time'), value_type=bool)\n    follower_yaml = os.path.join(get_package_share_directory('goal_pose_gui'), 'config', 'pose_follower.yaml')\n    return LaunchDescription([\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('robot_type', default_value='arm',\n                              description='arm, diff, ackermann, holonomic, legged or drone'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('planning_group', default_value='arm', description='MoveIt planning group (arms)'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('end_effector_link', default_value='', description='tool link (arms)'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('stamped', default_value='false',\n                              description='publish TwistStamped (Jazzy diff_drive_controller) instead of Twist'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('cmd_vel', default_value='/cmd_vel', description='velocity command topic'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('use_sim_time', default_value='true'),\n        Node(package='goal_pose_gui', executable='goal_pose_gui', name='goal_pose_gui', output='screen',\n             parameters=[{'robot_type': robot_type, 'planning_group': LaunchConfiguration('planning_group'),\n                          'end_effector_link': LaunchConfiguration('end_effector_link'), 'stamped': stamped,\n                          'use_sim_time': sim_time}],\n             remappings=[('cmd_vel', LaunchConfiguration('cmd_vel'))]),\n        Node(package='goal_pose_gui', executable='pose_follower', name='pose_follower', output='screen',\n             condition=UnlessCondition(PythonExpression([\"'\", robot_type, \"' == 'arm'\"])),\n             parameters=[follower_yaml, {'robot_type': robot_type, 'stamped': stamped, 'use_sim_time': sim_time}],\n             remappings=[('cmd_vel', LaunchConfiguration('cmd_vel'))]),\n    ])\n","package.xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<?xml-model href=\"http://download.ros.org/schema/package_format3.xsd\" schematypens=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\"?>\n<package format=\"3\">\n  <name>goal_pose_gui</name>\n  <version>1.0.0</version>\n  <description>\n    A separate window (like joint_state_publisher_gui) to type goal positions and orientations for any robot:\n    tool poses and joint values for arms (MoveIt move_group or a joint_trajectory_controller), goal poses and\n    velocities for mobile, legged and flying robots. Also pose_follower: drives a base to /goal_pose or a\n    /navigate_to_pose goal without Nav2.\n  </description>\n  <maintainer email=\"prasadprabhu@nitte.edu.in\">ROS2Lab</maintainer>\n  <license>Apache-2.0</license>\n\n  <exec_depend>rclpy</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>python_qt_binding</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>std_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>geometry_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>sensor_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>nav_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>nav2_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>moveit_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>control_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>trajectory_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>action_msgs</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>tf2_ros</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>urdfdom_py</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>launch</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>launch_ros</exec_depend>\n\n  <test_depend>python3-pytest</test_depend>\n\n  <export>\n    <build_type>ament_python</build_type>\n  </export>\n</package>\n","resource/goal_pose_gui":"","setup.cfg":"[develop]\nscript_dir=$base/lib/goal_pose_gui\n[install]\ninstall_scripts=$base/lib/goal_pose_gui\n","setup.py":"from glob import glob\nimport os\n\nfrom setuptools import find_packages, setup\n\npackage_name = 'goal_pose_gui'\n\nsetup(\n    name=package_name,\n    version='1.0.0',\n    packages=find_packages(exclude=['test']),\n    data_files=[\n        ('share/ament_index/resource_index/packages', ['resource/' + package_name]),\n        ('share/' + package_name, ['package.xml']),\n        (os.path.join('share', package_name, 'launch'), glob('launch/*.launch.py')),\n        (os.path.join('share', package_name, 'config'), glob('config/*.yaml')),\n    ],\n    install_requires=['setuptools'],\n    zip_safe=True,\n    maintainer='ROS2Lab',\n    maintainer_email='prasadprabhu@nitte.edu.in',\n    description='A goal window for any robot (arms, mobile, legged, flying) and a simple pose follower',\n    license='Apache-2.0',\n    tests_require=['pytest'],\n    entry_points={\n        'console_scripts': [\n            'goal_pose_gui = goal_pose_gui.gui:main',\n            'pose_follower = goal_pose_gui.pose_follower:main',\n        ],\n    },\n)\n","test/test_geometry.py":"import math\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom goal_pose_gui.geometry import (FollowerGains, follower_command, quaternion_from_rpy, rpy_from_quaternion,\n                                    wrap_angle)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('rpy', [(0, 0, 0), (0.3, -0.2, 1.0), (-1.2, 0.5, -2.9), (math.pi / 2 - 0.01, 0.1, 0.2)])\ndef test_rpy_round_trip(rpy):\n    q = quaternion_from_rpy(*rpy)\n    assert math.isclose(sum(c * c for c in q), 1.0, rel_tol=1e-12)\n    back = rpy_from_quaternion(*q)\n    for a, b in zip(rpy, back):\n        assert abs(wrap_angle(a - b)) < 1e-9\n\n\ndef test_yaw_quaternion():\n    x, y, z, w = quaternion_from_rpy(0, 0, math.pi / 2)\n    assert (round(x, 9), round(y, 9)) == (0, 0)\n    assert math.isclose(z, math.sqrt(0.5)) and math.isclose(w, math.sqrt(0.5))\n\n\ndef simulate(gains, goal, steps=4000, dt=0.05):\n    x = y = z = yaw = 0.0\n    aligning = False\n    for _ in range(steps):\n        vx, vy, vz, wz, aligning, done = follower_command((x, y, z, yaw), goal, gains, aligning)\n        if done:\n            return (x, y, z, yaw)\n        yaw += wz * dt\n        x += (vx * math.cos(yaw) - vy * math.sin(yaw)) * dt\n        y += (vx * math.sin(yaw) + vy * math.cos(yaw)) * dt\n        z += vz * dt\n    raise AssertionError('goal not reached')\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('goal', [(1.0, 0.5, 0.0, 0.0), (-0.8, 1.2, 0.0, 1.5), (0.2, -0.3, 0.0, -3.0)])\ndef test_differential_robot_reaches_goal(goal):\n    x, y, _, yaw = simulate(FollowerGains(), goal)\n    assert math.hypot(goal[0] - x, goal[1] - y) <= 0.08\n    assert abs(wrap_angle(goal[3] - yaw)) <= 0.05\n\n\ndef test_holonomic_and_flying():\n    g = FollowerGains(max_linear=0.5, holonomic=True, fly=True)\n    x, y, z, _ = simulate(g, (1.0, -1.0, 1.2, 0.7))\n    assert math.hypot(1.0 - x, -1.0 - y) <= 0.08 and abs(z - 1.2) <= 0.05\n\n\ndef test_speed_limits():\n    g = FollowerGains(max_linear=0.22, max_angular=1.5)\n    vx, vy, vz, wz, _, _ = follower_command((0, 0, 0, 0), (10, 0, 0, 0), g)\n    assert vx <= 0.22 + 1e-9 and abs(wz) <= 1.5 and vy == 0 and vz == 0\n\n\ndef test_car_rolls_while_it_steers_and_ignores_goal_yaw():\n    g = FollowerGains(max_linear=0.6, max_angular=0.8, car=True, min_radius=0.6)\n    pose = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n    for _ in range(4000):   # a goal to the side: a car has to drive an arc to get there\n        vx, vy, vz, wz, _, done = follower_command(tuple(pose), (0.0, 1.5, 0.0, 0.0), g)\n        if done:\n            break\n        assert vx != 0.0                       # never turns on the spot\n        assert abs(wz) <= abs(vx) / 0.6 + 1e-9  # never tighter than its turning radius\n        pose[2] = 0.0\n        pose[3] += wz * 0.02\n        pose[0] += vx * math.cos(pose[3]) * 0.02\n        pose[1] += vx * math.sin(pose[3]) * 0.02\n    assert done\n"},"ros2lab_hardware":{"CMakeLists.txt":"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.16)\nproject(ros2lab_hardware LANGUAGES CXX)\n\nif(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES \"(GNU|Clang)\")\n  add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic)\nendif()\n\nfind_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)\nfind_package(hardware_interface REQUIRED)\nfind_package(pluginlib REQUIRED)\nfind_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)\nfind_package(rclcpp_lifecycle REQUIRED)\n\nadd_library(ros2lab_hardware SHARED src/bridge_system.cpp src/transport.cpp)\ntarget_compile_features(ros2lab_hardware PUBLIC cxx_std_17)\ntarget_include_directories(ros2lab_hardware PUBLIC\n  $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>\n  $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:include/${PROJECT_NAME}>)\ntarget_link_libraries(ros2lab_hardware PUBLIC\n  hardware_interface::hardware_interface pluginlib::pluginlib rclcpp::rclcpp rclcpp_lifecycle::rclcpp_lifecycle)\npluginlib_export_plugin_description_file(hardware_interface ros2lab_hardware.xml)\n\n# a small command-line tool: talk to the board without ROS (bench tests, wiring checks)\nadd_executable(bridge_probe src/bridge_probe.cpp src/transport.cpp)\ntarget_include_directories(bridge_probe PRIVATE include)\ntarget_compile_features(bridge_probe PRIVATE cxx_std_17)\n\ninstall(DIRECTORY include/ DESTINATION include/${PROJECT_NAME})\ninstall(TARGETS ros2lab_hardware EXPORT export_${PROJECT_NAME}\n  ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib LIBRARY DESTINATION lib RUNTIME DESTINATION bin)\ninstall(TARGETS bridge_probe DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME})\ninstall(PROGRAMS scripts/ros2lab_robot_setup.py DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME} RENAME ros2lab_robot_setup)\ninstall(DIRECTORY config launch udev DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME})\n\nif(BUILD_TESTING)\n  find_package(ament_cmake_gtest REQUIRED)\n  ament_add_gtest(test_protocol test/test_protocol.cpp)\n  target_include_directories(test_protocol PRIVATE include)\n  ament_add_gtest(test_bridge_system test/test_bridge_system.cpp)\n  target_link_libraries(test_bridge_system ros2lab_hardware util)\nendif()\n\nament_export_targets(export_${PROJECT_NAME} HAS_LIBRARY_TARGET)\nament_export_dependencies(hardware_interface pluginlib rclcpp rclcpp_lifecycle)\nament_package()\n","README.md":"# ros2lab_hardware\n\nThe ros2_control driver for robots built with an ESP32 or Arduino Mega running the ROS2Lab bridge firmware.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Plugin | `ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem` (hardware_interface::SystemInterface) |\n| Joints | one command interface each: `position` (servos) or `velocity` (DC motors); state `position` (+ `velocity`) |\n| Sensors | an IMU with the 10 state interfaces of `imu_sensor_broadcaster` (orientation, angular velocity, acceleration) |\n| Link | USB serial (`transport: serial`, `device`, `baud`) or Wi-Fi UDP (`transport: udp`, `host`, `port`) |\n| Safety | the board only drives the motors after ENABLE and stops them 500 ms after the last command |\n\n## Files\n\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `config/bridge.ros2_control.xacro` | the macro `ros2lab_system`: one `<ros2_control>` block for `hardware_type:=mock`, `gz` or `real` |\n| `launch/bridge.launch.py` | robot_state_publisher + ros2_control_node + spawner for any robot on the bridge |\n| `scripts/ros2lab_robot_setup.py` | `ros2 run ros2lab_hardware ros2lab_robot_setup`: the ros2_control xacro, controllers.yaml, the firmware's robot_config.h and a wiring table, from the robot's URDF |\n| `src/bridge_probe.cpp` | `ros2 run ros2lab_hardware bridge_probe serial /dev/ros2lab_mcu 921600`: talk to the board without ROS |\n| `udev/99-ros2lab-mcu.rules` | a fixed name, `/dev/ros2lab_mcu`, for the usual USB-serial chips |\n| `test/` | gtest: the protocol, and the plugin against a fake board on a pseudo-terminal |\n\n## Use it\n\n```bash\nros2 run ros2lab_hardware ros2lab_robot_setup --package chiku_description --type diff --board esp32 --imu --out ~/chiku_hw\nros2 launch ros2lab_hardware bridge.launch.py robot_xacro:=<robot with its ros2_control xacro> \\\n    controllers_file:=~/chiku_hw/controllers.yaml controllers:=\"joint_state_broadcaster diff_drive_controller\" hardware_type:=real\n```\n\nThe course robots' `<robot>_bringup` packages do this for you: `ros2 launch <robot>_bringup bringup.launch.py hardware_type:=real`.\nOn ROS2Lab, real hardware needs a hardware license from the course administrator.\n","config/bridge.ros2_control.xacro":"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<!-- One <ros2_control> block for a ROS2Lab course robot, with the hardware chosen by hardware_type:\n       mock  mock_components/GenericSystem (fake hardware: commands are echoed as states)\n       gz    gz_ros2_control/GazeboSimSystem (Gazebo Harmonic)\n       real  ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem (the ESP32 / Arduino board over USB serial or Wi-Fi)\n     Use it from the robot's URDF:\n       <xacro:include filename=\"$(find ros2lab_hardware)/config/bridge.ros2_control.xacro\"/>\n       <xacro:ros2lab_system name=\"arm6\" hardware_type=\"$(arg hardware_type)\" transport=\"serial\" device=\"/dev/ros2lab_mcu\">\n         <interfaces>   (one wrapper element: its content becomes the <ros2_control> joints and sensors)\n           <joint name=\"joint1\"><command_interface name=\"position\"/><state_interface name=\"position\"/><state_interface name=\"velocity\"/></joint>\n           ...\n         </interfaces>\n       </xacro:ros2lab_system>   -->\n<robot xmlns:xacro=\"http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro\">\n  <xacro:macro name=\"ros2lab_system\" params=\"name hardware_type:=mock transport:=serial device:=/dev/ros2lab_mcu baud:=115200 host:=192.168.4.1 port:=8888 robot_id:='' **interfaces\">\n    <ros2_control name=\"${name}_system\" type=\"system\">\n      <hardware>\n        <xacro:if value=\"${hardware_type == 'mock'}\">\n          <plugin>mock_components/GenericSystem</plugin>\n          <param name=\"calculate_dynamics\">true</param>\n        </xacro:if>\n        <xacro:if value=\"${hardware_type == 'gz'}\">\n          <plugin>gz_ros2_control/GazeboSimSystem</plugin>\n        </xacro:if>\n        <xacro:if value=\"${hardware_type == 'real'}\">\n          <plugin>ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem</plugin>\n          <param name=\"transport\">${transport}</param>\n          <param name=\"device\">${device}</param>\n          <param name=\"baud\">${baud}</param>\n          <param name=\"host\">${host}</param>\n          <param name=\"port\">${port}</param>\n          <param name=\"robot_id\">${robot_id if robot_id else name}</param>\n        </xacro:if>\n      </hardware>\n      <xacro:insert_block name=\"interfaces\"/>\n    </ros2_control>\n  </xacro:macro>\n</robot>\n","launch/bridge.launch.py":"# Starts a robot that runs on the ROS2Lab bridge: robot_state_publisher, controller_manager (ros2_control_node) with\n# the ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem plugin (or mock_components for hardware_type:=mock), and the controller spawner.\n#   ros2 launch ros2lab_hardware bridge.launch.py robot_xacro:=<urdf.xacro> controllers_file:=<controllers.yaml> \\\n#       controllers:=\"joint_state_broadcaster diff_drive_controller\" hardware_type:=real transport:=serial device:=/dev/ros2lab_mcu\n# The course robots' <id>_bringup packages write the same three nodes out in their own launch/real.launch.py.\nimport xacro\nfrom launch import LaunchDescription\nfrom launch.actions import DeclareLaunchArgument, OpaqueFunction\nfrom launch.substitutions import LaunchConfiguration\nfrom launch_ros.actions import Node\nfrom launch_ros.parameter_descriptions import ParameterValue\n\nXACRO_ARGS = ('hardware_type', 'transport', 'device', 'host')\n# mecanum_drive_controller and the steering controllers publish odom -> base_link on ~/tf_odometry: send it to /tf\nTF_ODOM_CONTROLLERS = ('mecanum_drive_controller', 'ackermann_steering_controller')\n\n\ndef launch_setup(context):\n    get = lambda name: LaunchConfiguration(name).perform(context)  # noqa: E731\n    description = xacro.process_file(get('robot_xacro'), mappings={k: get(k) for k in XACRO_ARGS}).toxml()\n    controllers = get('controllers').split()\n    return [\n        Node(package='robot_state_publisher', executable='robot_state_publisher', output='screen',\n             parameters=[{'robot_description': ParameterValue(description, value_type=str)}]),\n        # Jazzy: controller_manager reads the URDF from the robot_description topic (robot_state_publisher)\n        Node(package='controller_manager', executable='ros2_control_node', output='screen',\n             parameters=[get('controllers_file')]),\n        Node(package='controller_manager', executable='spawner', output='screen',\n             arguments=controllers + ['--controller-manager', '/controller_manager', '--controller-manager-timeout', '30'] +\n             (['--controller-ros-args', '-r ~/tf_odometry:=/tf'] if set(controllers) & set(TF_ODOM_CONTROLLERS) else [])),\n    ]\n\n\ndef generate_launch_description():\n    return LaunchDescription([\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('robot_xacro', description='The robot URDF / xacro that includes its <id>.ros2_control.xacro'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('controllers_file', description='controllers.yaml (controller_manager and the controllers)'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('controllers', default_value='joint_state_broadcaster', description='Controllers to start, separated by spaces'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('hardware_type', default_value='real', choices=['mock', 'real'],\n                              description='real: the board through ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem; mock: mock_components/GenericSystem'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('transport', default_value='serial', choices=['serial', 'udp'], description='serial: USB; udp: Wi-Fi'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('device', default_value='/dev/ros2lab_mcu', description='Serial device (USB)'),\n        DeclareLaunchArgument('host', default_value='192.168.4.1', description=\"The board's IP address (Wi-Fi)\"),\n        OpaqueFunction(function=launch_setup),\n    ])\n","package.xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<?xml-model href=\"http://download.ros.org/schema/package_format3.xsd\" schematypens=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\"?>\n<package format=\"3\">\n  <name>ros2lab_hardware</name>\n  <version>1.0.0</version>\n  <description>\n    ros2_control hardware for the ROS2Lab course robots (arm3, arm6, chiku, mecanum, ackermann, quadruped, hexapod,\n    humanoid, mobile and legged manipulators): a C++ SystemInterface that talks to an ESP32 or Arduino board running\n    the ROS2Lab bridge firmware over USB serial or Wi-Fi (UDP). The board drives the servos and DC motors and reads\n    the encoders and the IMU.\n  </description>\n  <maintainer email=\"prasadprabhu@nitte.edu.in\">ROS2Lab</maintainer>\n  <license>Apache-2.0</license>\n\n  <buildtool_depend>ament_cmake</buildtool_depend>\n\n  <depend>hardware_interface</depend>\n  <depend>pluginlib</depend>\n  <depend>rclcpp</depend>\n  <depend>rclcpp_lifecycle</depend>\n\n  <exec_depend>controller_manager</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>robot_state_publisher</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>xacro</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>launch_ros</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>joint_state_broadcaster</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>joint_trajectory_controller</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>diff_drive_controller</exec_depend>\n  <exec_depend>imu_sensor_broadcaster</exec_depend>\n\n  <test_depend>ament_cmake_gtest</test_depend>\n\n  <export>\n    <build_type>ament_cmake</build_type>\n  </export>\n</package>\n","ros2lab_hardware.xml":"<library path=\"ros2lab_hardware\">\n  <class name=\"ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem\" type=\"ros2lab_hardware::BridgeSystem\" base_class_type=\"hardware_interface::SystemInterface\">\n    <description>\n      ROS2Lab course robots: joints and IMU of an ESP32 / Arduino board running the ROS2Lab bridge firmware,\n      over USB serial or Wi-Fi (UDP).\n    </description>\n  </class>\n</library>\n","scripts/ros2lab_robot_setup.py":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"ros2lab_robot_setup: everything a course robot needs to run on real hardware, generated from its URDF.\n\n  ros2 run ros2lab_hardware ros2lab_robot_setup --urdf robot.urdf --type diff --board esp32 --out ./out\n  ros2 run ros2lab_hardware ros2lab_robot_setup --package chiku_description --type diff        (uses urdf/<name>.urdf.xacro)\n\nWrites into --out (default ./ros2lab_<robot>):\n  <robot>.ros2_control.xacro   the <ros2_control> block (hardware_type:=mock|gz|real) to include in the URDF\n  controllers.yaml             controller_manager + controllers (joint_state_broadcaster, trajectory / drive controller)\n  robot_config.h               the firmware configuration (copy to firmware/ros2lab_bridge/ and flash)\n  WIRING.md                    which joint goes to which pin / channel\n\nRobot types: arm, diff, mecanum, ackermann, legged (quadruped, hexapod, humanoid), mobile_manipulator, legged_manipulator.\nBoards: esp32 (DevKitC; servos on a PCA9685, up to 2 DC motors) or mega (Arduino Mega 2560; up to 4 DC motors).\nCheck every pin against your own wiring before powering the motors.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport os\nimport secrets\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n\nTYPES = ('arm', 'diff', 'mecanum', 'ackermann', 'legged', 'mobile_manipulator', 'legged_manipulator')\n\n# default wiring: the pins the generated firmware uses (see hardware/SPECS.md for the parts)\nPINS = {\n    'esp32': {\n        'motors': [  # TB6612FNG: PWM, IN1, IN2; encoder A, B (any input with pull-up)\n            dict(driver='TB6612', pwm=25, b=26, c=27, ea=18, eb=19),\n            dict(driver='TB6612', pwm=33, b=32, c=4, ea=16, eb=17),\n        ],\n        'servo_pins': [],                  # ESP32: every servo goes through the PCA9685 (I2C SDA 21, SCL 22)\n        'pca_channels': 32,                # two PCA9685 boards: 0x40 and 0x41\n        'baud': 921600,\n        'sts': dict(port='Serial2', rx=13, tx=14),   # Feetech bus (via a half-duplex bus-servo adapter)\n    },\n    'mega': {\n        'motors': [  # TB6612FNG / L298N: PWM, IN1, IN2; encoder A on an interrupt pin (2, 3, 18, 19), B any pin\n            dict(driver='TB6612', pwm=5, b=22, c=23, ea=2, eb=30),\n            dict(driver='TB6612', pwm=6, b=24, c=25, ea=3, eb=31),\n            dict(driver='TB6612', pwm=7, b=26, c=27, ea=18, eb=32),\n            dict(driver='TB6612', pwm=8, b=28, c=29, ea=19, eb=33),\n        ],\n        'servo_pins': [9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 34, 35, 36, 37, 38, 39, 40],   # Servo library (up to 12 on timer 5)\n        'pca_channels': 32,\n        'baud': 500000,                    # 16 MHz AVR: 500 kbit/s is exact (115200 is 2 % off and too slow for 100 Hz)\n        'sts': dict(port='Serial2', rx=17, tx=16),   # RX2 17, TX2 16\n    },\n}\n# DC motor: a 12 V gear motor with a Hall encoder (e.g. JGB37-520, 11 lines, 1:30): 11 x 2 x 30 counts per output turn\nDEFAULT_MOTOR = dict(counts_per_rev=660.0, kp=0.08, ki=0.6, kd=0.0, max_vel=20.0)\n# hobby servo (MG996R): 500..2500 us over its 180 deg travel, centre 1500 us = 0 rad; speed about 5 rad/s at no load\nDEFAULT_SERVO = dict(us_min=500, us_max=2500, travel=math.pi, max_speed=5.0)   # travel: pi for a 180 deg servo, 4.712 for 270 deg\n\n\ndef xacro_to_urdf(path):\n    out = subprocess.run(['xacro', path], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    return out.stdout\n\n\ndef load_urdf(args):\n    if args.urdf:\n        text = open(args.urdf, encoding='utf-8').read()\n        return xacro_to_urdf(args.urdf) if 'xmlns:xacro' in text else text\n    from ament_index_python.packages import get_package_share_directory\n    share = get_package_share_directory(args.package)\n    urdf_dir = os.path.join(share, 'urdf')\n    files = sorted(f for f in os.listdir(urdf_dir) if f.endswith(('.urdf.xacro', '.urdf', '.xacro')))\n    if not files:\n        sys.exit(f'No .urdf / .urdf.xacro in {urdf_dir}')\n    main = next((f for f in files if not re.search(r'(gazebo|control|sim|macro|common)', f)), files[0])\n    path = os.path.join(urdf_dir, main)\n    return xacro_to_urdf(path) if main.endswith('xacro') else open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\n\ndef parse(urdf_text):\n    root = ET.fromstring(urdf_text)\n    links = {link.get('name'): link for link in root.findall('link')}\n    joints = []\n    for j in root.findall('joint'):\n        if j.get('type') not in ('revolute', 'continuous', 'prismatic') or j.find('mimic') is not None:\n            continue\n        lim = j.find('limit')\n        lo, hi = (-math.pi, math.pi)\n        if j.get('type') != 'continuous' and lim is not None:\n            lo, hi = float(lim.get('lower', lo)), float(lim.get('upper', hi))\n        org = j.find('origin')\n        xyz = [float(v) for v in (org.get('xyz', '0 0 0') if org is not None else '0 0 0').split()]\n        joints.append(dict(name=j.get('name'), type=j.get('type'), lower=lo, upper=hi, xyz=xyz,\n                           child=j.find('child').get('link')))\n    children = {j.find('child').get('link') for j in root.findall('joint') if j.find('child') is not None}\n    base = next((n for n in links if n not in children), 'base_link')   # the root link: the robot's base frame\n    return root.get('name'), joints, links, base\n\n\ndef wheel_radius(links, link_name):\n    link = links.get(link_name)\n    if link is None:\n        return None\n    for tag in ('collision', 'visual'):\n        for el in link.findall(tag):\n            cyl = el.find('geometry/cylinder')\n            if cyl is not None:\n                return float(cyl.get('radius'))\n            sph = el.find('geometry/sphere')\n            if sph is not None:\n                return float(sph.get('radius'))\n    return None\n\n\ndef plan(name, joints, links, kind, board, servo='pwm', sts_ids=None):\n    \"\"\"Which joint is a motor and which a servo, and on which pins.\"\"\"\n    is_wheel = lambda j: j['type'] == 'continuous' or re.search(r'wheel', j['name'])  # noqa: E731\n    is_steer = lambda j: re.search(r'steer', j['name'])  # noqa: E731\n    wheels = [j for j in joints if is_wheel(j) and not is_steer(j)]\n    others = [j for j in joints if j not in wheels]\n    if kind in ('diff', 'mecanum', 'ackermann', 'mobile_manipulator') and not wheels:\n        sys.exit('No wheel joints found (continuous joints, or names with \"wheel\")')\n    motors, servos, passive = [], [], []\n    if kind in ('diff', 'mecanum', 'mobile_manipulator', 'ackermann'):\n        motors = [j for j in wheels if not re.search(r'caster', j['name'])]\n        servos = [j for j in others if not re.search(r'caster', j['name'])]\n        if kind == 'ackermann':\n            # rear-wheel drive: the front wheels roll freely on the steering knuckles (passive joints: in ros2_control\n            # with a state only, so they still have a TF, but not on the board)\n            rear = [j for j in motors if re.search(r'rear|back', j['name'])] or [j for j in motors if j['xyz'][0] < 0]\n            if rear:\n                passive = [j for j in motors if j not in rear]\n                motors = rear\n    else:\n        servos = others + wheels\n    P = PINS[board]\n    if len(motors) > len(P['motors']):\n        sys.exit(f'{len(motors)} DC motors, but the {board} plan has pins for {len(P[\"motors\"])}: use --board mega')\n    out = []\n    for i, j in enumerate(motors):\n        out.append(dict(joint=j, actuator='motor', pins=P['motors'][i], index=i))\n    if servo == 'sts':\n        ids = dict(sts_ids or {})\n        unknown = set(ids) - {j['name'] for j in servos}\n        if unknown:\n            sys.exit(f'--sts-ids names joints that are not servos: {\", \".join(sorted(unknown))}')\n        free = (i for i in range(1, 254) if i not in ids.values())\n        for j in servos:\n            out.append(dict(joint=j, actuator='sts', bus_id=ids[j['name']] if j['name'] in ids else next(free)))\n        return out + [dict(joint=j, actuator='passive') for j in passive]\n    use_pca = board == 'esp32' or len(servos) > len(P['servo_pins'])\n    if use_pca and len(servos) > P['pca_channels']:\n        sys.exit(f'{len(servos)} servos: more than two PCA9685 boards hold')\n    for i, j in enumerate(servos):\n        out.append(dict(joint=j, actuator='servo', pca=use_pca, channel=i if use_pca else None,\n                        pin=None if use_pca else P['servo_pins'][i]))\n    return out + [dict(joint=j, actuator='passive') for j in passive]\n\n\ndef ros2_control_xacro(name, plan_, imu, board):\n    lines = [\n        '<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>',\n        f'<!-- {name}: ros2_control for mock / Gazebo / the real robot (ros2lab_hardware). Generated by ros2lab_robot_setup. -->',\n        '<robot xmlns:xacro=\"http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro\">',\n        '  <xacro:arg name=\"hardware_type\" default=\"mock\"/>',\n        '  <xacro:arg name=\"transport\" default=\"serial\"/>',\n        '  <xacro:arg name=\"device\" default=\"/dev/ros2lab_mcu\"/>',\n        '  <xacro:arg name=\"host\" default=\"192.168.4.1\"/>',\n        '  <xacro:include filename=\"$(find ros2lab_hardware)/config/bridge.ros2_control.xacro\"/>',\n        f'  <xacro:ros2lab_system name=\"{name}\" hardware_type=\"$(arg hardware_type)\" transport=\"$(arg transport)\" '\n        f'device=\"$(arg device)\" baud=\"{PINS[board][\"baud\"]}\" host=\"$(arg host)\" robot_id=\"{name}\">',\n        '    <interfaces>',\n    ]\n    for p in plan_:\n        j = p['joint']\n        if p['actuator'] == 'passive':   # state only: robot_state_publisher still gets its TF\n            lines += [f'      <joint name=\"{j[\"name\"]}\">', '        <state_interface name=\"position\"/>', '      </joint>']\n            continue\n        cmd = 'velocity' if p['actuator'] == 'motor' else 'position'\n        init = '' if cmd == 'velocity' else f'<param name=\"initial_value\">{0.0 if j[\"lower\"] <= 0 <= j[\"upper\"] else (j[\"lower\"] + j[\"upper\"]) / 2:.3f}</param>'\n        lines.append(f'      <joint name=\"{j[\"name\"]}\">')\n        lines.append(f'        <command_interface name=\"{cmd}\"/>')\n        lines.append(f'        <state_interface name=\"position\">{init}</state_interface>')\n        lines.append('        <state_interface name=\"velocity\"/>')\n        lines.append('      </joint>')\n    if imu:\n        lines.append('      <sensor name=\"imu\">')\n        for f in ('orientation.x', 'orientation.y', 'orientation.z', 'orientation.w', 'angular_velocity.x', 'angular_velocity.y',\n                  'angular_velocity.z', 'linear_acceleration.x', 'linear_acceleration.y', 'linear_acceleration.z'):\n            lines.append(f'        <state_interface name=\"{f}\"/>')\n        lines.append('      </sensor>')\n    lines += ['    </interfaces>', '  </xacro:ros2lab_system>', '</robot>', '']\n    return '\\n'.join(lines)\n\n\ndef controllers_yaml(name, kind, plan_, links, imu, base='base_link'):  # noqa: C901\n    motors = [p['joint'] for p in plan_ if p['actuator'] == 'motor']\n    servos = [p['joint'] for p in plan_ if p['actuator'] not in ('motor', 'passive')]\n    ctl = {'joint_state_broadcaster': 'joint_state_broadcaster/JointStateBroadcaster'}\n    body = []\n    if imu:\n        ctl['imu_sensor_broadcaster'] = 'imu_sensor_broadcaster/IMUSensorBroadcaster'\n        body.append(f'imu_sensor_broadcaster:\\n  ros__parameters:\\n    sensor_name: imu\\n    frame_id: {base}\\n')\n    if kind in ('diff', 'mobile_manipulator') and motors:\n        left = [j['name'] for j in motors if j['xyz'][1] > 0]\n        right = [j['name'] for j in motors if j['xyz'][1] <= 0]\n        sep = (max(j['xyz'][1] for j in motors) - min(j['xyz'][1] for j in motors)) if len(motors) > 1 else 0.3\n        r = wheel_radius(links, motors[0]['child']) or 0.05\n        ctl['diff_drive_controller'] = 'diff_drive_controller/DiffDriveController'\n        body.append(f'''diff_drive_controller:\n  ros__parameters:\n    left_wheel_names: {left}\n    right_wheel_names: {right}\n    wheel_separation: {sep:.4f}\n    wheel_radius: {r:.4f}\n    publish_rate: 50.0\n    odom_frame_id: odom\n    base_frame_id: {base}\n    enable_odom_tf: true\n    cmd_vel_timeout: 0.5\n    linear.x.max_velocity: 0.5\n    angular.z.max_velocity: 2.0\n''')\n    if kind == 'mecanum' and len(motors) == 4:\n        order = sorted(motors, key=lambda j: (-j['xyz'][0], -j['xyz'][1]))   # front left, front right, rear left, rear right\n        fl, fr, rl, rr = order[0], order[1], order[2], order[3]\n        r = wheel_radius(links, fl['child']) or 0.04\n        lx, ly = abs(fl['xyz'][0]), abs(fl['xyz'][1])\n        ctl['mecanum_drive_controller'] = 'mecanum_drive_controller/MecanumDriveController'\n        body.append(f'''mecanum_drive_controller:\n  ros__parameters:\n    reference_timeout: 0.5\n    front_left_wheel_command_joint_name: {fl['name']}\n    front_right_wheel_command_joint_name: {fr['name']}\n    rear_left_wheel_command_joint_name: {rl['name']}\n    rear_right_wheel_command_joint_name: {rr['name']}\n    kinematics:\n      base_frame_offset: {{x: 0.0, y: 0.0, theta: 0.0}}\n      wheels_radius: {r:.4f}\n      sum_of_robot_center_projection_on_X_Y_axis: {lx + ly:.4f}\n    base_frame_id: {base}\n    odom_frame_id: odom\n''')\n    if kind == 'ackermann':\n        steer_j = [j for j in servos if re.search(r'steer', j['name'])]\n        steer = [j['name'] for j in steer_j]\n        right_first = lambda js: [j['name'] for j in sorted(js, key=lambda j: j['xyz'][1])]  # noqa: E731\n        span = lambda js: (max(j['xyz'][1] for j in js) - min(j['xyz'][1] for j in js)) if len(js) > 1 else 0.2  # noqa: E731\n        wheelbase = (sum(j['xyz'][0] for j in steer_j) / len(steer_j) - sum(j['xyz'][0] for j in motors) / len(motors)) if steer_j and motors else 0.3\n        r = (wheel_radius(links, motors[0]['child']) if motors else None) or 0.05\n        ctl['ackermann_steering_controller'] = 'ackermann_steering_controller/AckermannSteeringController'\n        body.append(f'''ackermann_steering_controller:\n  ros__parameters:\n    reference_timeout: 0.5\n    front_steering: true\n    open_loop: false\n    velocity_rolling_window_size: 10\n    position_feedback: true\n    base_frame_id: {base}\n    odom_frame_id: odom\n    traction_joints_names: {right_first(motors)}\n    steering_joints_names: {right_first(steer_j)}\n    wheelbase: {abs(wheelbase):.4f}\n    traction_track_width: {span(motors):.4f}\n    steering_track_width: {span(steer_j):.4f}\n    traction_wheels_radius: {r:.4f}\n''')\n        servos = [j for j in servos if j['name'] not in steer]\n    if servos:\n        ctl['joint_trajectory_controller'] = 'joint_trajectory_controller/JointTrajectoryController'\n        body.append('joint_trajectory_controller:\\n  ros__parameters:\\n    joints:\\n' + ''.join(f'      - {j[\"name\"]}\\n' for j in servos) +\n                    '    command_interfaces: [position]\\n    state_interfaces: [position, velocity]\\n    allow_partial_joints_goal: false\\n'\n                    '    constraints:\\n      stopped_velocity_tolerance: 0.05\\n      goal_time: 0.0\\n')\n    head = 'controller_manager:\\n  ros__parameters:\\n    update_rate: 100\\n' + ''.join(f'    {k}:\\n      type: {v}\\n' for k, v in ctl.items())\n    return f'# {name}: ros2_control controllers. Generated by ros2lab_robot_setup.\\n' + head + '\\n' + '\\n'.join(body)\n\n\ndef firmware_config(name, plan_, board, imu, wifi, wifi_pass=None):\n    P = PINS[board]\n    lines = [f'// robot_config.h for {name} ({board}): generated by ros2lab_robot_setup. Check every pin against your wiring.',\n             '#pragma once', '#include \"bridge_core.h\"', '#include \"actuators.h\"', '#include \"imu.h\"', '',\n             f'#define ROBOT_ID \"{name}\"', f'#define BRIDGE_BAUD {P[\"baud\"]}']\n    if wifi and board == 'esp32':\n        lines += ['#define WIFI_AP                     // the robot makes its own Wi-Fi; remove for the lab network', f'#define WIFI_SSID \"{name}_robot\"',\n                  f'#define WIFI_PASS \"{wifi_pass or new_password()}\"   // made for this robot; the Jetson joins with it', '#define UDP_PORT 8888']\n    lines.append('')\n    servos = [p for p in plan_ if p['actuator'] == 'servo']\n    sts = [p for p in plan_ if p['actuator'] == 'sts']\n    if any(p.get('pca') for p in servos):\n        lines.append('static bridge::Pca9685 pca0(0x40), pca1(0x41);')\n    if sts:\n        lines.append(f'static bridge::StsBus sts({P[\"sts\"][\"port\"]});   // Feetech STS3215 bus, 1 Mbit/s')\n    if any(p['actuator'] == 'motor' for p in plan_):\n        lines.append(f'static const bridge::MotorTuning MOTOR = {{{DEFAULT_MOTOR[\"counts_per_rev\"]}f, {DEFAULT_MOTOR[\"kp\"]}f, {DEFAULT_MOTOR[\"ki\"]}f, '\n                     f'{DEFAULT_MOTOR[\"kd\"]}f, {DEFAULT_MOTOR[\"max_vel\"]}f, false, false}};   // counts/rev, kp, ki, kd, max rad/s, position mode, invert')\n    lines.append('')\n    lines.append('static void robot_setup(bridge::Actuator ** a, uint8_t & n, bridge::Imu *& imu)')\n    lines.append('{')\n    if any(p.get('pca') for p in servos):\n        lines.append('  pca0.begin();' + ('\\n  pca1.begin();' if any((p.get('channel') or 0) >= 16 for p in servos) else ''))\n    if sts:\n        lines.append(f'  sts.begin({P[\"sts\"][\"rx\"]}, {P[\"sts\"][\"tx\"]});')\n    lines.append('  n = 0;')\n    for p in plan_:\n        j = p['joint']\n        if p['actuator'] == 'sts':\n            var = re.sub(r'\\W', '_', j['name'])\n            lo, hi = j['lower'], j['upper']\n            lines.append(f'  static bridge::StsServo s_{var}(sts, {p[\"bus_id\"]}, 2048, 1, {lo:.3f}f, {hi:.3f}f);   // {j[\"name\"]}: '\n                         'raw 2048 = 0 rad; calibrate the offset per servo')\n            lines.append(f'  a[n++] = &s_{var};')\n        elif p['actuator'] == 'motor':\n            m = p['pins']\n            pins = f'{{bridge::Driver::{m[\"driver\"]}, {m[\"pwm\"]}, {m[\"b\"]}, {m[\"c\"]}, {m[\"ea\"]}, {m[\"eb\"]}}}'\n            lines.append(f'  static bridge::DcMotor m{p[\"index\"]}({p[\"index\"]}, {pins}, MOTOR);   // {j[\"name\"]}')\n            lines.append(f'  a[n++] = &m{p[\"index\"]};')\n        elif p['actuator'] == 'servo':\n            half = DEFAULT_SERVO['travel'] / 2   # a joint cannot go past the servo's own travel\n            lo, hi = max(j['lower'], -half), min(j['upper'], half)\n            rng = (f'{{{DEFAULT_SERVO[\"us_min\"]}, {DEFAULT_SERVO[\"us_max\"]}, {DEFAULT_SERVO[\"travel\"]:.4f}f, {lo:.3f}f, {hi:.3f}f, '\n                   f'{DEFAULT_SERVO[\"max_speed\"]}f, false, 0.0f}}')\n            init = 0.0 if lo <= 0 <= hi else (lo + hi) / 2\n            var = re.sub(r'\\W', '_', j['name'])\n            if p['pca']:\n                board_ = 'pca0' if p['channel'] < 16 else 'pca1'\n                lines.append(f'  static bridge::ServoPca9685 s_{var}({board_}, {p[\"channel\"] % 16}, {rng}, {init:.3f}f);   // {j[\"name\"]}')\n            else:\n                lines.append(f'  static bridge::ServoPwm s_{var}({p[\"pin\"]}, {rng}, {init:.3f}f);   // {j[\"name\"]}')\n            lines.append(f'  a[n++] = &s_{var};')\n    if imu:\n        lines.append('  static bridge::Mpu6050 mpu;   // or bridge::Bno055 bno; (I2C)')\n        lines.append('  imu = &mpu;')\n    else:\n        lines.append('  imu = 0;   // no IMU on this board (add one: --imu)')\n    lines.append('}')\n    lines.append('')\n    return '\\n'.join(lines)\n\n\ndef new_password():\n    return 'r2l-' + secrets.token_urlsafe(9)\n\n\ndef i2c_note(plan_, i2c, imu):\n    parts = (['PCA9685 servo board(s) (0x40, 0x41)'] if any(p.get('pca') for p in plan_) else []) + \\\n        (['IMU (MPU-6050 0x68 or BNO055 0x28)'] if imu else [])\n    return f'I2C ({i2c}): {\", \".join(parts)}.\\n' if parts else ''\n\n\ndef sts_note(plan_, board):\n    if not any(p['actuator'] == 'sts' for p in plan_):\n        return ''\n    b = PINS[board]['sts']\n    return (f'Feetech bus: board {b[\"port\"]} (RX {b[\"rx\"]}, TX {b[\"tx\"]}) to a half-duplex bus-servo adapter (Waveshare Bus Servo '\n            'Adapter or the Feetech FE-URT-1 in TTL mode), 1 Mbit/s; servo supply 7.4 V (or 12 V for the 12 V STS3215). '\n            'Give every servo its ID first (Feetech FD software, one servo on the bus at a time), then set each offset so '\n            'that the URDF zero pose reads 0 rad.\\n')\n\n\ndef wiring_md(name, plan_, board, imu):\n    rows = []\n    for p in plan_:\n        j = p['joint']['name']\n        if p['actuator'] == 'motor':\n            m = p['pins']\n            rows.append(f'| {j} | DC motor + encoder ({m[\"driver\"]}) | PWM {m[\"pwm\"]}, IN1 {m[\"b\"]}, IN2 {m[\"c\"]} | encoder A {m[\"ea\"]}, B {m[\"eb\"]} |')\n        elif p['actuator'] == 'sts':\n            rows.append(f'| {j} | Feetech STS3215 bus servo | bus ID {p[\"bus_id\"]} | position + speed (bus) |')\n        elif p['actuator'] == 'passive':\n            rows.append(f'| {j} | none (rolls freely) | - | - |')\n        elif p['pca']:\n            rows.append(f'| {j} | servo | PCA9685 {\"0x40\" if p[\"channel\"] < 16 else \"0x41\"} channel {p[\"channel\"] % 16} | - |')\n        else:\n            rows.append(f'| {j} | servo | pin {p[\"pin\"]} | - |')\n    i2c = 'SDA 21, SCL 22' if board == 'esp32' else 'SDA 20, SCL 21'\n    return f'''# {name}: wiring ({board})\n\n| Joint | Actuator | Output | Feedback |\n|---|---|---|---|\n{chr(10).join(rows)}\n\n{i2c_note(plan_, i2c, imu)}{sts_note(plan_, board)}\nPower: servos and motors from their own battery / regulator (never from the board's 5 V pin); connect all grounds.\nJoint order = the order of the <ros2_control> block = the order in robot_config.h. Do not reorder one without the other.\n'''\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    src = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n    src.add_argument('--urdf', help='a .urdf or .urdf.xacro file')\n    src.add_argument('--package', help='a description package (its urdf/ folder)')\n    ap.add_argument('--type', required=True, choices=TYPES)\n    ap.add_argument('--board', default='esp32', choices=sorted(PINS))\n    ap.add_argument('--servo', default='pwm', choices=('pwm', 'sts'),\n                    help='pwm: hobby servos (PCA9685 or board pins); sts: Feetech STS3215 serial bus servos')\n    ap.add_argument('--sts-ids', default='', help='bus IDs, e.g. shoulder_pan=1,shoulder_lift=2 (default: 1, 2, ... in joint order)')\n    ap.add_argument('--imu', action='store_true', help='the board has an IMU (MPU-6050 / BNO055)')\n    ap.add_argument('--wifi', action='store_true', help='ESP32: talk over Wi-Fi (UDP) as well as USB')\n    ap.add_argument('--wifi-pass', help='ESP32 Wi-Fi password (default: a new random one)')\n    ap.add_argument('--name', help='robot id (default: the URDF robot name)')\n    ap.add_argument('--out', help='output folder')\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    urdf = load_urdf(a)\n    robot, joints, links, base = parse(urdf)\n    name = a.name or robot\n    try:\n        ids = {k.strip(): int(v) for k, v in (x.split('=') for x in a.sts_ids.split(',') if x.strip())}\n    except ValueError:\n        sys.exit('--sts-ids: use joint=id pairs, e.g. shoulder_pan=1,shoulder_lift=2')\n    plan_ = plan(name, joints, links, a.type, a.board, a.servo, ids)\n    out = a.out or f'ros2lab_{name}'\n    os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)\n    files = {f'{name}.ros2_control.xacro': ros2_control_xacro(name, plan_, a.imu, a.board),\n             'controllers.yaml': controllers_yaml(name, a.type, plan_, links, a.imu, base),\n             'robot_config.h': firmware_config(name, plan_, a.board, a.imu, a.wifi, a.wifi_pass),\n             'WIRING.md': wiring_md(name, plan_, a.board, a.imu)}\n    for f, text in files.items():\n        with open(os.path.join(out, f), 'w', encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n            fh.write(text)\n    print(f'{name}: {sum(p[\"actuator\"] == \"motor\" for p in plan_)} DC motors, {sum(p[\"actuator\"] in (\"servo\", \"sts\") for p in plan_)} servos'\n          f'{\", %d passive joints\" % sum(p[\"actuator\"] == \"passive\" for p in plan_) if any(p[\"actuator\"] == \"passive\" for p in plan_) else \"\"} -> {out}/')\n    for f in files:\n        print(f'  {f}')\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n","udev/99-ros2lab-mcu.rules":"# ROS2Lab bridge boards: a stable name /dev/ros2lab_mcu for the USB-serial chip of the ESP32 / Arduino board.\n# Install:  sudo cp 99-ros2lab-mcu.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/ && sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger\n# Access: members of the dialout group (sudo usermod -aG dialout $USER, then log in again).\n#\n# Chips that lidars use too (Silicon Labs CP210x: RPLIDAR A1/C1, LDROBOT adapters; FTDI) must be matched by their serial\n# number, or /dev/ros2lab_mcu could point at the lidar. Find the board's serial with the board plugged in:\n#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyUSB0 | grep '{serial}' | head -1\n# then remove the # in front of the matching line below and put the serial in.\n#\n# Silicon Labs CP2102 / CP2104 (many ESP32 DevKitC boards): by serial only\n#SUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"10c4\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"ea60\", ATTRS{serial}==\"PUT_THE_SERIAL_HERE\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\n# FTDI FT232R: by serial only\n#SUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"0403\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"6001\", ATTRS{serial}==\"PUT_THE_SERIAL_HERE\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\n# WCH CH340 / CH341 (cheap ESP32 and Arduino clones)\nSUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"1a86\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"7523\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\n# WCH CH9102 (newer ESP32 boards)\nSUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"1a86\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"55d4\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\n# Espressif native USB (ESP32-S3 / ESP32-C3 USB-Serial/JTAG)\nSUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"303a\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"1001\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\n# Arduino Mega 2560 / Uno R3 (ATmega16U2)\nSUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"2341\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"0042\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\nSUBSYSTEM==\"tty\", ATTRS{idVendor}==\"2341\", ATTRS{idProduct}==\"0043\", SYMLINK+=\"ros2lab_mcu\", GROUP=\"dialout\", MODE=\"0660\", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}=\"1\"\n"},"ros2lab_firmware":{"README.md":"# ros2lab_bridge firmware\n\nThe program on the robot's microcontroller. It sits between the Jetson (ROS 2 Jazzy, `ros2_control`) and the\nrobot's servos, DC motors, encoders and IMU. The Jetson side is the C++ plugin `ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem`.\n\n| Board | Link to the Jetson | Arduino IDE 2 board | Libraries |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ESP32 DevKitC (ESP32-WROOM-32), ESP32-S3 | USB serial 921600 baud, and/or Wi-Fi UDP port 8888 | *ESP32 Dev Module* (Arduino-ESP32 core 3.x) | none |\n| Arduino Mega 2560 | USB serial 500000 baud | *Arduino Mega or Mega 2560* | *Servo* (only for servos on board pins) |\n\n## Files\n\n| File | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `ros2lab_bridge.ino` | serial and Wi-Fi links, the 200 Hz control loop |\n| `bridge_core.h` | the board's logic: HELLO, COMMAND, STATE, ENABLE, PING, the 500 ms watchdog |\n| `bridge_proto.h` | the frame format (same bytes as `ros2lab_hardware/protocol.hpp`) |\n| `actuators.h`, `actuators.cpp` | hobby servos on pins or a PCA9685, Feetech STS3215 bus servos, DC motors with encoders and PID (TB6612FNG, L298N, BTS7960) |\n| `imu.h` | MPU-6050 (complementary filter) and BNO055 (on-chip fusion) |\n| `robot_config.h` | **your robot**: which joint is which actuator, on which pins. Not in this folder: generate it |\n| `examples/` | generated configs: an SO-101 on the Feetech bus (ESP32), a two-wheel robot on a Mega, a PCA9685 arm over Wi-Fi |\n\n## Build and flash\n\n1. Generate the robot's files on the Jetson (or any ROS 2 computer):\n   ```bash\n   ros2 run ros2lab_hardware ros2lab_robot_setup --package <robot>_description --type <arm|diff|mecanum|ackermann|legged|...> \\\n       --board esp32 [--servo sts --sts-ids shoulder_pan=1,...] [--imu] [--wifi] --out ~/<robot>_hw\n   ```\n2. Copy `~/<robot>_hw/robot_config.h` into this folder (next to `ros2lab_bridge.ino`).\n3. Open `ros2lab_bridge.ino` in the Arduino IDE, choose the board and port, and upload.\n4. With the board on USB and nothing moving: `ros2 run ros2lab_hardware bridge_probe serial /dev/ros2lab_mcu 921600`\n   prints the robot id, the joint count and live joint states.\n\n## The protocol\n\nFrames are `0xAA 0x55 type length payload CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE` (little-endian floats). The Jetson sends `HELLO`, then\n`ENABLE 1`, then a `COMMAND` (one float per joint, in the joint order of the `<ros2_control>` block) every control\ncycle; the board answers each command with a `STATE` (time, position and velocity per joint, optional IMU). If no\ncommand arrives for 500 ms, the board switches the motors off and sends a `FAULT`; the next command switches them on\nagain. A `COMMAND` with the wrong joint count is refused with a `FAULT`.\n\n## What was checked, and what was not\n\n- Arduino Mega 2560: compiled with avr-gcc 7.3 and the Arduino AVR core 1.8.6 for a two-wheel robot (encoders, PID,\n  IMU) and for a six-servo STS3215 arm: no errors, no warnings (about 14 to 19 KB of flash).\n- ESP32: compiled only against small host stand-ins for the Arduino-ESP32 API (`test/stubs`), not with the real ESP32\n  toolchain. Build it in the Arduino IDE once before you rely on it.\n- `test/test_interop.cpp`: the firmware core and the Jetson's protocol code talk to each other byte for byte\n  (handshake, enable, commands, the watchdog, noise on the line).\n- `test/fake_board.cpp`: the firmware core with simulated joints on a pseudo-terminal. With it, the real ROS 2 Jazzy\n  stack (controller_manager 4.49, ros2_controllers 4.43) ran `ros2lab_hardware/BridgeSystem` end to end:\n  diff_drive_controller, mecanum_drive_controller and ackermann_steering_controller moved their joints and published\n  odometry, and imu_sensor_broadcaster published the IMU.\n  `./fake_board /tmp/ros2lab_mcu chiku vv imu`, then launch with `device:=/tmp/ros2lab_mcu`.\n- Not tested on real hardware here. Start with the robot lifted or the arm clear of everything, at low speed.\n"}};
